<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tynwald</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tynwald Court</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tynwald is the parliament of the Isle of Man, which descends from the Norse assembly, or thing, of the Kingdom of Mann and the Isles and claims a continuous existence of more than a thousand years. Each year on 5 July it holds an open-air sitting at Tynwald Hill in St John's, where new laws are proclaimed in English and Manx.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tynwald.jpg" alt="Tynwald" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Junior Jumper · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Legislative_Council_of_the_Isle_of_Man_as_of_Apr_2020.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
